1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,320
Hello and welcome back to JD Science.

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:05,180
Today we are exploring hormones.

3
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:10,100
Hormones are chemical messengers released by endocrine glands into

4
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:10,780
the bloodstream.

5
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:13,800
They are slower than nerves but last longer.

6
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:17,960
The pancreas makes insulin, the adrenal gland makes adrenaline,

7
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:22,120
the pituitary makes FSH and LH, the testes

8
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:25,760
make testosterone, and the ovaries make estrogen and

9
00:00:25,760 --> 00:00:26,500
progesterone.

10
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:28,920
The pituitary is the master gland.

11
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:32,720
In type 1 diabetes, the pancreas does not make

12
00:00:32,720 --> 00:00:35,260
enough insulin and insulin is injected.

13
00:00:35,780 --> 00:00:39,560
In type 2, the body doesn't respond well to insulin and

14
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:41,740
it is managed through diet and exercise.

15
00:00:42,480 --> 00:00:46,520
The menstrual cycle involves FSH, LH, estrogen

16
00:00:46,520 --> 00:00:47,820
and progesterone.

17
00:00:48,280 --> 00:00:51,920
FSH matures an egg, LH triggers ovulation

18
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:54,800
and progesterone maintains the uterus lining.

19
00:00:54,800 --> 00:00:58,440
When water is low, ADH is released and the

20
00:00:58,440 --> 00:01:00,300
kidney reabsorbs more water.

21
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:04,660
The endocrine system releases hormones into the bloodstream and

22
00:01:04,660 --> 00:01:07,080
only cells with suitable receptors respond.

23
00:01:07,640 --> 00:01:11,640
The pituitary coordinates several glands but hormone control

24
00:01:11,640 --> 00:01:15,340
involves feed loops rather than a single gland acting alone.

25
00:01:16,040 --> 00:01:19,940
Type 1 diabetes usually involves autoimmune destruction of

26
00:01:19,940 --> 00:01:21,700
insulin producing beta cells.

27
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:25,420
Type 2 diabetes involves insulin resistance and may

28
00:01:25,420 --> 00:01:27,840
the also involve reduced insulin production.

29
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:32,300
Treatment varies and may include medicines as well as lifestyle measures.

30
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:36,640
As you revise this topic, try to explain the key process in

31
00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:37,600
your own words.

32
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:42,020
Focus on what happens, why it happens and how the structures

33
00:01:42,020 --> 00:01:43,460
involved help the process.

34
00:01:44,400 --> 00:01:48,460
Now pause the video and try this exam style question.

35
00:01:48,460 --> 00:01:52,340
Name the hormone that triggers ovulation and state which gland

36
00:01:52,340 --> 00:01:53,160
produces it.

37
00:01:53,660 --> 00:01:57,780
Here is a model answer LH luteinizing hormone produced

38
00:01:57,780 --> 00:01:59,200
by the pituitary gland.

